1
00:00:03,980 --> 00:00:06,340
I carry high my craven flag,

2
00:00:06,560 --> 00:00:11,277
my ally I'm gonna fly and let my
struggles shoot me through the sky!

3
00:00:11,360 --> 00:00:14,997
It'd be a pity if we
lingered here and let our

4
00:00:15,080 --> 00:00:18,057
pretty sparks of life
blend aloud and disappear?

5
00:00:18,140 --> 00:00:23,137
There may be fog that even
you can't navigate If someone

6
00:00:23,220 --> 00:00:25,837
strong like you is lost then
who will set me straight?

7
00:00:25,920 --> 00:00:28,697
Cause when the waves
cast, my heart exists?

8
00:00:28,780 --> 00:00:30,737
It's been your kindness and your strength!

9
00:00:30,820 --> 00:00:33,057
That would free me from the mist.

10
00:00:33,140 --> 00:00:34,860
And just like that!

11
00:00:35,840 --> 00:00:37,800
We move on.

12
00:00:38,480 --> 00:00:40,637
Sail to a new dawn.

13
00:00:40,720 --> 00:00:43,317
Weigh anchor, ride as high as you can!

14
00:00:43,400 --> 00:00:45,437
I assure I don't need anger.

15
00:00:45,520 --> 00:00:47,577
I go fast as I am, yeah.

16
00:00:47,660 --> 00:00:50,637
I hear you laughing like
you're numb to it all?

17
00:00:50,720 --> 00:00:52,617
Well, we're dashing together!

18
00:00:52,700 --> 00:00:55,077
No, we're never gonna fall, you know!

19
00:00:55,160 --> 00:00:57,617
The whole world may now be my enemy?

20
00:00:57,700 --> 00:01:01,580
Water swirl, but I ain't backing
down so long as I'm free!

21
00:01:02,300 --> 00:01:05,157
Thought I'll give it, come
round the current with me.

22
00:01:05,240 --> 00:01:09,800
All in, wake up bright and
early, making for the peak we go!

23
00:01:19,660 --> 00:01:24,320
All in, wake up bright and
early, making for the peak we go!

24
00:01:45,740 --> 00:01:49,000
I don't know.

25
00:01:55,320 --> 00:02:00,260
Dark is the sky.

26
00:02:03,160 --> 00:02:07,200
Fierce is the storm.

27
00:02:08,200 --> 00:02:10,740
The wind blows.

28
00:02:15,080 --> 00:02:17,880
At Onikachiwa.

29
00:02:23,980 --> 00:02:28,797
Oh, the dragon roars.

30
00:02:28,880 --> 00:02:35,340
The howling beasts sing feasting merrily.

31
00:02:41,380 --> 00:02:45,997
Beneath the autumn leaves.

32
00:02:46,080 --> 00:02:49,740
Dreams become reality.

33
00:02:51,080 --> 00:02:54,177
At Habu Port.

34
00:02:54,260 --> 00:02:57,800
The bold take to the sea.

35
00:03:02,780 --> 00:03:06,017
The retainers of Kozuki Odin.

36
00:03:06,100 --> 00:03:07,897
Returned at long last.

37
00:03:07,980 --> 00:03:10,497
To battle they go.

38
00:03:10,580 --> 00:03:13,100
A story of true loyalty.

39
00:03:15,320 --> 00:03:16,150
So,

40
00:03:16,520 --> 00:03:21,457
please allow me to

41
00:03:21,540 --> 00:03:25,320
tell this tale modestly.

42
00:03:32,040 --> 00:03:38,520
Our story begins on a dark,
stormy night not long ago.

43
00:03:39,860 --> 00:03:42,320
One day before this year's Fire Festival.

44
00:03:44,660 --> 00:03:47,200
Meanwhile, not far from
the flower capital,

45
00:03:47,760 --> 00:03:50,457
Momonosuke and his friends
head toward Tokage Port?

46
00:03:50,540 --> 00:03:53,011
hoping to catch Luffy before he sets sail.

47
00:03:54,720 --> 00:03:57,437
So, you've changed your
mind about going to sea?

48
00:03:57,520 --> 00:03:58,350
Uh-huh.

49
00:03:58,433 --> 00:03:59,263
At least for now.

50
00:03:59,346 --> 00:04:01,197
And I've already told Luffy about it.

51
00:04:01,280 --> 00:04:02,517
You truly want to stay?

52
00:04:02,600 --> 00:04:03,430
I'm surprised.

53
00:04:03,560 --> 00:04:04,390
You want me gone?

54
00:04:04,473 --> 00:04:05,303
Not at all.

55
00:04:05,420 --> 00:04:07,717
On the contrary, it's
reassuring to have you.

56
00:04:07,800 --> 00:04:12,447
But when we last spoke, you told me that
you had come to an important decision.

57
00:04:13,260 --> 00:04:16,660
Well, Odin started his journey
by traveling across Wano.

58
00:04:16,960 --> 00:04:18,666
I haven't even done that yet.

59
00:04:19,060 --> 00:04:21,660
So I decided to follow his path properly.

60
00:04:21,960 --> 00:04:24,117
I'll go out to see when the time is right.

61
00:04:24,200 --> 00:04:28,137
That's fine, but I can't believe Luffy
discussed his departure with you.

62
00:04:28,220 --> 00:04:31,817
Or more specifically, I can't believe
he failed to discuss it with me.

63
00:04:31,900 --> 00:04:32,730
That traitor!

64
00:04:32,860 --> 00:04:35,757
He's leaving without saying
goodbye to me and Kin'emon!

65
00:04:35,840 --> 00:04:37,340
I don't understand!

66
00:04:42,680 --> 00:04:43,760
What's your name?

67
00:04:46,640 --> 00:04:49,020
Your father was a fool of a lord.

68
00:04:52,080 --> 00:04:53,900
Tell me, who are you?

69
00:04:54,100 --> 00:04:56,360
And why are you here? Oh, me?

70
00:04:56,540 --> 00:04:59,364
Luffy, I'm gonna be king
of the pirates someday.

71
00:05:00,120 --> 00:05:01,260
Cut the crap!

72
00:05:01,500 --> 00:05:03,197
I don't care if you're a samurai!

73
00:05:03,280 --> 00:05:06,960
I'm gonna be king of the
pirates someday! Ha! So what?

74
00:05:07,160 --> 00:05:09,257
I shall be the Shogun of Wado someday!

75
00:05:09,340 --> 00:05:11,811
and you'll be like a worm beneath my feet!

76
00:05:12,020 --> 00:05:14,120
I'm not a worm or an eel!

77
00:05:14,380 --> 00:05:15,677
Then you're a monkey, you saint!

78
00:05:15,760 --> 00:05:16,590
What?

79
00:05:16,673 --> 00:05:17,503
These are awesome!

80
00:05:18,320 --> 00:05:19,377
What are you?

81
00:05:19,460 --> 00:05:21,160
A figurehead, huh, Momo?

82
00:05:23,580 --> 00:05:25,100
You just gonna cry?

83
00:05:27,700 --> 00:05:30,640
I want to vanquish Emmerichino!

84
00:05:33,160 --> 00:05:34,440
Hey, Momo.

85
00:05:36,040 --> 00:05:37,340
Let's team up.

86
00:05:38,160 --> 00:05:38,990
Moffey!

87
00:05:43,340 --> 00:05:44,170
Hey, Momo!

88
00:05:45,440 --> 00:05:47,280
It's okay, I know!

89
00:05:47,700 --> 00:05:50,760
You're just a little crybaby
with a dumb top knot!

90
00:05:51,080 --> 00:05:52,786
What are you gonna do anyway?

91
00:05:53,040 --> 00:05:54,746
Nothing, and you know it too!

92
00:05:55,040 --> 00:05:57,080
Gotta find a way to survive, okay?

93
00:05:57,440 --> 00:06:00,300
Just hang on, and we'll come rescue you!

94
00:06:03,320 --> 00:06:04,980
Because you're my friend!

95
00:06:05,760 --> 00:06:09,340
Now, brat, one last time.

96
00:06:09,840 --> 00:06:11,680
What is your name?

97
00:06:12,320 --> 00:06:14,240
You want my name?

98
00:06:14,460 --> 00:06:16,820
It's Kozuki Morinoste!

99
00:06:17,260 --> 00:06:18,800
Hear me now!

100
00:06:19,220 --> 00:06:24,640
I shall become the Shogun
of the Land of Plano!

101
00:06:27,640 --> 00:06:28,680
So fly!

102
00:06:29,980 --> 00:06:33,700
With your eyes open this time, I shall.

103
00:06:35,120 --> 00:06:39,140
Your job is to stop Onigashima.

104
00:06:43,280 --> 00:06:46,120
As for Kaido, I got this.

105
00:06:47,140 --> 00:06:48,400
Hear that?

106
00:06:48,980 --> 00:06:50,640
You're done for!

107
00:06:54,540 --> 00:06:56,500
We've had our share of quarrels.

108
00:06:56,680 --> 00:06:59,739
But does our adventure
together mean nothing to you?

109
00:07:00,340 --> 00:07:04,017
There is a limit to how much
boorishness I can tolerate.

110
00:07:04,100 --> 00:07:07,041
You're confusing personal
freedom with disrespect!

111
00:07:07,360 --> 00:07:08,920
Right, Tinemon? Indeed.

112
00:07:09,320 --> 00:07:10,555
Well spoken, my lord.

113
00:07:10,740 --> 00:07:14,681
But if you don't mind, I must ask,
why do you run when you can fly?

114
00:07:15,360 --> 00:07:16,840
Silence! Yes, sir.

115
00:07:17,060 --> 00:07:18,960
I apologize for my insolence.

116
00:07:20,040 --> 00:07:23,460
Now, Sir Luffy must answer
for disrespecting our Shogun.

117
00:07:23,580 --> 00:07:28,051
If he cannot explain his vile actions
to us, we shall consider him an enemy.

118
00:07:28,280 --> 00:07:30,220
Yes, that is the way of samurai!

119
00:07:30,700 --> 00:07:33,417
Know that it is you who
trampled on our friendship,

120
00:07:33,500 --> 00:07:35,157
Luffy, He saved the whole country.

121
00:07:35,240 --> 00:07:36,077
Give him a break.

122
00:07:36,160 --> 00:07:36,990
I will not.

123
00:07:37,073 --> 00:07:38,480
He humiliated me.

124
00:07:38,900 --> 00:07:39,959
I will strike him,

125
00:07:40,160 --> 00:07:45,500
then fight him, and then make him pay
in whatever manner I deem most suitable.

126
00:07:50,780 --> 00:07:53,237
Remember, we're enemies
the next time I see you.

127
00:07:53,320 --> 00:07:54,597
Don't try to be friendly.

128
00:07:54,680 --> 00:07:56,621
If you do, you might end up dead.

129
00:07:57,340 --> 00:07:59,140
Okay, that's fine with me.

130
00:07:59,400 --> 00:08:00,660
See you, Traffy!

131
00:08:01,200 --> 00:08:02,030
Shut up.

132
00:08:03,020 --> 00:08:04,880
I'll see you around, Jaggy.

133
00:08:05,060 --> 00:08:07,160
I can't wait to kick your ass.

134
00:08:07,980 --> 00:08:09,720
Time to set sail!

135
00:08:12,940 --> 00:08:13,820
Your hope?

136
00:08:14,020 --> 00:08:14,860
No, me!

137
00:08:15,580 --> 00:08:16,410
Finally.

138
00:08:24,860 --> 00:08:26,640
How dare you!

139
00:08:27,720 --> 00:08:29,140
Stop right there!

140
00:08:29,920 --> 00:08:30,877
Hi, guys!

141
00:08:30,960 --> 00:08:32,860
We came here to send you off.

142
00:08:48,820 --> 00:08:52,157
What were you thinking running
off without saying a word to us?

143
00:08:52,240 --> 00:08:56,887
Kin'emon and I have known you for longer
than anyone else in Wano you scoundrel.

144
00:08:57,380 --> 00:08:59,740
You have deeply offended the both of us.

145
00:08:59,900 --> 00:09:01,397
You better have a good excuse.

146
00:09:01,480 --> 00:09:03,068
Well, you're seeing me now.

147
00:09:03,440 --> 00:09:05,160
Listen to me.

148
00:09:05,560 --> 00:09:08,020
This is an order from the Shogun.

149
00:09:08,620 --> 00:09:09,450
Okay.

150
00:09:14,700 --> 00:09:16,400
Please don't go.

151
00:09:17,020 --> 00:09:19,340
You make me so sad.

152
00:09:22,860 --> 00:09:25,417
I want to stay with all of you. I don't...

153
00:09:25,500 --> 00:09:27,420
I don't know what I'll do!

154
00:09:28,180 --> 00:09:30,700
I don't think I can make it without you!

155
00:09:48,660 --> 00:09:50,836
You're the reason I was able to live!

156
00:09:51,220 --> 00:09:52,917
You gave me the strength to fight!

157
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:57,540
You all were the reason
I was able to smile again

158
00:09:59,040 --> 00:10:02,040
Thank you for avenging
my father and mother

159
00:10:03,040 --> 00:10:05,320
Thank you for saving my country

160
00:10:07,260 --> 00:10:11,417
I am a fool So I struggle
to put this into words

161
00:10:11,500 --> 00:10:15,940
But I fear what is to come
I need you here with me

162
00:10:17,260 --> 00:10:22,280
He's not very Shogun-like He's
still a kid Give him a break

163
00:10:25,800 --> 00:10:26,630
Usopp!

164
00:10:27,800 --> 00:10:28,630
Right!

165
00:10:28,713 --> 00:10:30,520
Ready to go! Incoming!

166
00:10:34,620 --> 00:10:37,537
We were waiting on the Sunny
so we could give you this.

167
00:10:37,620 --> 00:10:39,400
So don't Shoguns order me.

168
00:10:40,200 --> 00:10:42,817
You got bigger, but I
know you're still a kid.

169
00:10:42,900 --> 00:10:44,897
You're also a dumb little scaredy-cat.

170
00:10:44,980 --> 00:10:46,000
And a crybaby.

171
00:10:50,200 --> 00:10:54,680
But you know you're like
a little brother to me.

172
00:10:59,240 --> 00:11:02,537
What is this your flag?

173
00:11:02,620 --> 00:11:06,157
If things get tough we've
still got your back!

174
00:11:06,240 --> 00:11:08,517
Fly that flag to send a message!

175
00:11:08,600 --> 00:11:11,677
If bad guys see that it'll send a packet!

176
00:11:11,760 --> 00:11:12,677
I promise you!

177
00:11:12,760 --> 00:11:15,397
Messing with our friend means?

178
00:11:15,480 --> 00:11:20,009
He's messing with us, and the Straw Hat
Pirates don't back down from a fight!

179
00:11:23,880 --> 00:11:24,997
Your friend...

180
00:11:25,080 --> 00:11:26,580
I'm one of you!

181
00:11:42,400 --> 00:11:43,600
Kinema! Yamato!

182
00:11:47,160 --> 00:11:49,572
Momo, if you guys want to become pirates,

183
00:11:49,680 --> 00:11:53,915
we'll come and pick you up anytime,
but not if you're just going to cry.

184
00:12:02,480 --> 00:12:03,440
Set sail!

185
00:12:26,960 --> 00:12:28,980
Yama 2, stay tuned!

186
00:12:29,560 --> 00:12:31,360
Of course! See ya!

187
00:12:31,820 --> 00:12:34,520
Keep it super proud! We shall!

188
00:12:34,980 --> 00:12:36,980
Make me proud out there, show god!

189
00:12:37,220 --> 00:12:38,820
Good luck for my new stage!

190
00:12:39,400 --> 00:12:42,106
Go easy on the crying
and you'll do just fine!

191
00:12:44,440 --> 00:12:46,280
Remember to have fun, okay?

192
00:12:47,040 --> 00:12:48,511
We'll meet again someday.

193
00:12:48,760 --> 00:12:50,340
So take care until then!

194
00:13:25,460 --> 00:13:30,040
I will grow stronger each day
till I surpass Kozuki Oden.

195
00:13:34,280 --> 00:13:36,380
I know you'll make him proud.

196
00:13:36,920 --> 00:13:38,580
Surpass me! Will you stop!

197
00:13:46,540 --> 00:13:48,320
Okay, to Hakumai.

198
00:13:48,540 --> 00:13:49,599
We're not leaving?

199
00:13:49,760 --> 00:13:51,257
That's their official port.

200
00:13:51,340 --> 00:13:54,516
They have a lift there to
lower our ship to sea level.

201
00:13:54,980 --> 00:13:56,260
Oh, thank goodness.

202
00:13:56,680 --> 00:13:58,517
I did not care for the waterfall.

203
00:13:58,600 --> 00:14:01,247
My bones were quaking
just thinking about it.

204
00:14:05,880 --> 00:14:08,704
Straw Hatch, where are
you and Trafalgar off to?

205
00:14:08,820 --> 00:14:11,996
Are you going to use the
official port to leave water?

206
00:14:12,840 --> 00:14:14,857
That sounds nice and peaceful.

207
00:14:14,940 --> 00:14:16,857
It's a good choice for you.

208
00:14:16,940 --> 00:14:17,997
Average pirates.

209
00:14:18,080 --> 00:14:19,777
Don't blame you one bit.

210
00:14:19,860 --> 00:14:22,160
You guys gotta stay safe, right?

211
00:14:25,940 --> 00:14:27,297
Stay safe.

212
00:14:27,380 --> 00:14:28,517
You amateurs.

213
00:14:28,600 --> 00:14:30,200
Should take it easy.

214
00:14:31,780 --> 00:14:32,610
Easy.

215
00:14:35,580 --> 00:14:37,257
It's good to be safe.

216
00:14:37,340 --> 00:14:38,497
Don't take the bait.

217
00:14:38,580 --> 00:14:40,197
I don't like that look on your face.

218
00:14:40,280 --> 00:14:41,110
Captain?

219
00:14:41,193 --> 00:14:43,000
The official port is there for a reason.

220
00:14:43,180 --> 00:14:44,520
Shut up and follow me.

221
00:14:44,720 --> 00:14:45,550
To hell and back!

222
00:14:45,633 --> 00:14:46,497
Switch sides!

223
00:14:46,580 --> 00:14:48,051
You're an enabler, Beppo!

224
00:14:48,140 --> 00:14:49,757
Chief Bay, let me take the helm!

225
00:14:49,840 --> 00:14:51,680
No, don't listen to him!

226
00:14:51,920 --> 00:14:52,861
Captain, please!

227
00:14:53,420 --> 00:14:54,250
We are!

228
00:15:08,840 --> 00:15:14,020
Lord Momonosuke's allies flew into
battle like gods of vengeance.

229
00:15:14,500 --> 00:15:15,897
Tearing through lesser foes,

230
00:15:15,980 --> 00:15:21,317
they reached to the sky where they
faced the Dragon King Kaido himself.

231
00:15:21,400 --> 00:15:24,740
A monstrous Oiran stood beside him.

232
00:15:24,860 --> 00:15:26,180
But even with her aid,

233
00:15:26,420 --> 00:15:28,757
the dragon could not
withstand the winds of

234
00:15:28,840 --> 00:15:31,620
change that blew at the
backs of our heroes.

235
00:15:35,880 --> 00:15:39,980
But nearby, despite being burned,
Orochi had not met his end.

236
00:15:41,880 --> 00:15:47,260
Brimming with contempt, he targeted our
princess Hiyori, who stood her ground.

237
00:15:49,880 --> 00:15:51,300
Then whoosh!

238
00:15:52,480 --> 00:15:53,310
Slash!

239
00:15:53,520 --> 00:15:57,440
The vile serpent was felled
in one cut! But by who?

240
00:15:57,800 --> 00:16:01,260
Why, Lord Odin's loyal retainer, Denjiro!

241
00:16:02,640 --> 00:16:05,300
Odinji's final head was set ablaze!

242
00:16:05,900 --> 00:16:10,540
The enemy of the Kozuki clan
paid for his treachery at last!

243
00:16:12,740 --> 00:16:14,097
Thunder roared!

244
00:16:14,180 --> 00:16:18,040
Kaido and Onigashima
itself were next to fall.

245
00:16:21,400 --> 00:16:25,580
For twenty years, dark clouds
had covered the land of Wano,

246
00:16:25,800 --> 00:16:27,500
blackening the entire realm.

247
00:16:29,300 --> 00:16:33,820
But then, suddenly, the
clouds began to clear.

248
00:16:35,200 --> 00:16:38,460
In the flower capital,
the festival carried on.

249
00:16:38,780 --> 00:16:41,960
Its lively music floated
into the night sky.

250
00:16:47,400 --> 00:16:52,280
But the snake lived, even
severed from its neck.

251
00:16:52,600 --> 00:16:57,840
The head of Oruji glared with spite,
and from its mouth, a warning came.

252
00:16:59,880 --> 00:17:04,177
The grudge of the Kurozumi clan will curse

253
00:17:04,260 --> 00:17:08,160
the land of Wano for generations to come.

254
00:17:08,420 --> 00:17:12,060
Your victory is but a force.

255
00:17:12,940 --> 00:17:14,840
Princess Hiyori stood firm,

256
00:17:15,180 --> 00:17:18,517
remembering the twenty years of
suffering her people had endured.

257
00:17:18,600 --> 00:17:20,940
She returned the serpent's glare.

258
00:17:21,380 --> 00:17:24,440
Lady Hiyori, stay away, cried Denjiro.

259
00:17:24,760 --> 00:17:26,540
But she would not be deterred.

260
00:17:27,660 --> 00:17:31,660
Our brave princess didn't flinch
in the face of the serpent's curse.

261
00:17:31,960 --> 00:17:34,440
She delivered his obituary!

262
